Files taken from the original without changes:
  agents/grader.md, agents/comparator.md, agents/analyzer.md,
  assets/eval_review.html, scripts/__init__.py, scripts/utils.py,
  scripts/package_skill.py

Files taken from the original and modified (each carries a notice at the top):
  scripts/aggregate_benchmark.py  - candidate-first config ordering (correct delta sign
                                    for old_skill/new_skill); computed runs_per_configuration
  eval-viewer/generate_review.py  - finds eval_metadata.json for the run-N layout
  references/schemas.md           - added contents list and layout note
  scripts/run_eval.py             - agent-neutral "command" runner (any agent CLI) and --trigger-regex
  scripts/run_loop.py             - passes the runner and --llm-cmd options through; --model optional
  scripts/improve_description.py  - --llm-cmd for any LLM CLI; prompt no longer assumes Claude Code
  scripts/generate_report.py      - agent-neutral wording in the report text
  eval-viewer/viewer.html         - agent-neutral wording in user-facing text
  scripts/quick_validate.py       - nested-SKILL.md message framed around hosted
                                    upload targets instead of claude.ai alone

Made agent-neutral (default code paths no longer require Claude Code):
  scripts/run_eval.py             - runner registry; --runner defaults to auto
                                    (command via --agent-cmd or
                                    $SKILL_EVAL_AGENT_CMD, else claude-code when
                                    `claude` is on PATH, else an actionable error);
                                    `claude` still accepted as an alias
  scripts/run_loop.py             - same runner registry and auto default
  scripts/improve_description.py  - LLM CLI auto-detected from a known list;
                                    no `claude -p` default
  scripts/validate_skill.py       - declarative CLIENTS registry replaces ~20
                                    hardcoded Claude Code branches; CC-SUBST
                                    renamed CLIENT-SUBST
  scripts/init_skill.py           - same CLIENTS registry pattern
  scripts/vet_skill.py            - docstring says "some clients" instead of
                                    naming Claude Code for !`command` injection

Reference-visibility pass (version 1.2.0; the routing material that tells an
agent which bundled file to open, and the checks and teaching that go with it):
  SKILL.md                       - routing paragraph at the top, a "Read first"
                                    column in the request-routing table, an
                                    imperative gate at the head of every phase that
                                    has a reference file, and a bottom section
                                    retitled as an index of what the skill bundles
                                    rather than a load order
  scripts/validate_skill.py       - new REF-PASSIVE check: a bundled reference or
                                    agent brief named in SKILL.md but never gated
                                    by an instruction to open it
  references/quality-rubric.md    - two structure items, on reference reachability
                                    and on summaries pointing at rather than
                                    restating their reference
  references/writing-guide.md     - "Progressive disclosure that gets read" under
                                    Part 2, and a form-to-failure row for skipping
                                    a reference and improvising the procedure
  evals/evals.json                - per-eval assertions that the reference for the
                                    phase under test was opened before the work

SKILL.md was rewritten, and incorporates the original's eval, grading, and
description-optimization workflow. All other files are new.

